From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 23:40:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/25] Broadcast reload-agents notification over presence
 WebSocket
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Push a reload-agents message to every connected TUI client over the
existing presence WebSocket after /global/reload-agents succeeds.
The TUI re-fetches its agent list on receipt, so the Task tool's
subagent-type registry picks up newly-enabled agents without
restarting the engine.

Server: broadcastReload() in presence.ts mirrors _broadcast() exactly
— module-scoped, cross-worktree by construction.

Client: presence-client.ts handles incoming {type:"reload-agents"}
messages, calling the new onReloadAgents callback. sdk.tsx wires it
to synthesize a global.agents-reloaded event through the existing
handleEvent pipeline, reusing the sync.tsx agent-list re-fetch.

The reloadAll() functions in agent/skill/command continue to use
Instance.directories() (unchanged from patch 0004) — the broadcast
is additive, not a replacement.
